  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The General Services Administration obligated $1.2B in contracts in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 135,796 awards with an average award size of $8.9K, and obligations fell 95.8% year over year. FY2027 to date sits well below recent full fiscal-year totals: FY26 obligations were $28.9B, FY25 were $23.8B, FY24 were $26.5B, FY23 were $23.9B, and FY22 were $20.6B. Computer Systems Design Services leads FY2027 to date category spending with $240M, followed by Engineering Services with $172M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $84.3M. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $91M in obligations, followed by MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC with $64.5M and V2X AEROSPACE LLC with $49.1M. Other notable categories and vendors include Software Publishers ($67.2M) and PERATON INC. ($45.4M). These figures cover fiscal year to date obligations and reflect partial current-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $1.2B in FY2027 to date, down 95.8% year over year. Award activity totaled 135,796 awards with an average award size of $8.9K. This partial-year total contrasts with full-year obligations of $28.9B in FY26 and $26.5B in FY24."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors lead FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest category with $240M, followed by Engineering Services with $172M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $84.3M. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC leads vendors with $91M, followed by MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC with $64.5M and V2X AEROSPACE LLC with $49.1M."
      }
